{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The kos.</b> The owl (סויאט״ה); it hides from human eyes and dwells in uninhabited places." "<b>The shalach.</b> The pelican (קורמייאש״ה); it casts its young." "<b>The yanshuf.</b> The bat (קבנ״ט); it flies at twilight (נשף)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The transliterated Old French term סויאט״ה is read here as designating the owl; exact vernacular identification uncertain.", 1 "The Old French term קורמייאש״ה is read as designating the pelican; exact vernacular identification uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:18.476987178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}